        "Abstract": "This paper presents a method to construct a large-scale, high-quality Japanese web corpus for training Japanese large language models (LLMs). The corpus is extracted and refined from the Common Crawl archive, resulting in approximately 312.1 billion characters. Experiments demonstrate that continual pre-training on popular LLMs using the presented corpus improves their performance on Japanese benchmark datasets."
